msgid ""
"While the example above works great, it will pause all source streams "
"until they are needed. If you don't want that to happen, you can set "
"`pauseStreams` to `false`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:48
msgid ""
"However, what if you don't have all the source streams yet, or you don't "
"want to allocate the resources (file descriptors, memory, etc.) for them "
"right away? Well, in that case you can simply provide a callback that "
"supplies the stream by calling a `next()` function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:68
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:70
msgid "CombinedStream.create([options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:72
msgid "Returns a new combined stream object. Available options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:74
msgid "`maxDataSize`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:75
msgid "`pauseStreams`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:77
msgid "The effect of those options is described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:79
msgid "combinedStream.pauseStreams = `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:81
msgid ""
"Whether to apply back pressure to the underlaying streams. If set to "
"`false`, the underlaying streams will never be paused. If set to `true`, "
"the underlaying streams will be paused right after being appended, as "
"well as when `delayedStream.pipe()` wants to throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:86
msgid "combinedStream.maxDataSize = `2 * 1024 * 1024`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:88
msgid ""
"The maximum amount of bytes (or characters) to buffer for all source "
"streams. If this value is exceeded, `combinedStream` emits an `'error'` "
"event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:91
msgid "combinedStream.dataSize = `0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:93
msgid ""
"The amount of bytes (or characters) currently buffered by "
"`combinedStream`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:95
msgid "combinedStream.append(stream)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:97
msgid ""
"Appends the given `stream` to the combinedStream object. If "
"`pauseStreams` is set to `true, this stream will also be paused right "
"away."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:100
msgid ""
"`streams` can also be a function that takes one parameter called `next`. "
"`next` is a function that must be invoked in order to provide the `next` "
"stream, see example above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:104
msgid ""
"Regardless of how the `stream` is appended, combined-stream always "
"attaches an `'error'` listener to it, so you don't have to do that "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:107
msgid "Special case: `stream` can also be a String or Buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:109
msgid "combinedStream.write(data)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:111
msgid ""
"You should not call this, `combinedStream` takes care of piping the "
"appended streams into itself for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:114
msgid "combinedStream.resume()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:116
msgid ""
"Causes `combinedStream` to start drain the streams it manages. The "
"function is idempotent, and also emits a `'resume'` event each time which"
" usually goes to the stream that is currently being drained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:120
msgid "combinedStream.pause();"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:122
msgid ""
"If `combinedStream.pauseStreams` is set to `false`, this does nothing. "
"Otherwise a `'pause'` event is emitted, this goes to the stream that is "
"currently being drained, so you can use it to apply back pressure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:126
msgid "combinedStream.end();"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:128
msgid ""
"Sets `combinedStream.writable` to false, emits an `'end'` event, and "
"removes all streams from the queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:131
msgid "combinedStream.destroy();"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/combined-stream_Readme.md:133
msgid ""
"Same as `combinedStream.end()`, except it emits a `'close'` event instead"
" of `'end'`."
msgstr ""

